    "summary": "Overall school team award: Top 4 finalist = 9 pts, Top 1/3 = 3 pts, Top 1/2 = 1 pt. Individual best result counted once.",
    "rawText": "Aggregate Team Award\r\n\n\t\tTournament Goal\n\nThe Aggregate Team Award is meant to highlight the groups who attend AG Open with a team showcasing both:\r\n\nPerformance: Ability to make it to the top of the tournaments.\n\nDepth: The combined performance of the school as a whole, rather than a single stand-out individual of the school.\n\nScoring\n\nEach individual will have their best result considered, and their points added to their team's score.\r\n\nTop 4 of tournament (finalist): 9 points\n\nTop 1/3 of tournament: 3 points\n\nTop 1/2 of tournament: 1 point\n\nThe Team Aggregate score is the sum of all of the team member's contributions. Bringing more people to the event is always a good thing. 🙂\r\n\nNote: Each individual is counted once. If you win 3 gold medals you are a pretty awesome individual and having a fantastic weekend. But still only contribute 9 points to your team.\n\n(An individual's Longsword Relay result does count towards the Aggregate Team Score, unless the individual is on one of the mixed school pickup teams, or on a school team that has elected to compete in Tier-B)",
    "rawHtml": ""
